  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening of Humanitarian Hubs in North-East Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2016, IOM in Nigeria has managed and supported humanitarian hubs in eight locations across Borno State, including Maiduguri, Gwoza, Bama, Ngala, Dikwa, Monguno, Banki, and Damasak. These hubs play a critical enabling role in the provision of life-saving humanitarian assistance by improving access to the more than 7 million people in need of assistance in north-east Nigeria. However, in order to mitigate the risk posed by insecurity in the region, in the wake of recent physical attacks on the hubs, this project is contributing to the repairs and maintenance of the hubs premise and the enhancement of power generation through solar. Through this project IOM is strengthening the humanitarian field hubs&#x2019; sustainability to ensure continued provision of the hubs&#x2019; services, including accommodation, training/meeting facilities, office space and access to internet and telecommunication services for humanitarian responders by upgrading and improving the infrastructure of hubs in Gwoza, Bama, Dikwa, and Monguno, in regard to repair of damages and solar power provision.</narrative>
  </description>
